1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,043
Coding agents, 60s:

2
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:05,254
before, you paste your chatbot's code and never stop,

3
00:00:05,254 --> 00:00:08,704
but how does 1 agent loop 4 steps until you're done?

4
00:00:09,204 --> 00:00:11,416
Here's how, in one story: a mechanic.

5
00:00:12,366 --> 00:00:14,453
A chatbot is the mechanic on the phone.

6
00:00:14,753 --> 00:00:15,848
He can only talk.

7
00:00:16,148 --> 00:00:19,597
So you paste his fix, run it, and carry the error back to him.

8
00:00:20,546 --> 00:00:24,263
A coding agent is the same mechanic, in your garage, with tools.

9
00:00:24,563 --> 00:00:27,178
You give it one job, in your terminal or editor.

10
00:00:27,478 --> 00:00:28,615
It reads your files.

11
00:00:28,915 --> 00:00:29,889
It edits the code.

12
00:00:30,189 --> 00:00:32,037
It runs a command, and checks the result.

13
00:00:32,337 --> 00:00:33,201
Still broken?

14
00:00:33,501 --> 00:00:35,976
It goes around again, until the job is done.

15
00:00:36,476 --> 00:00:40,074
That's the answer I promised: one agent, one loop, four steps.

16
00:00:40,374 --> 00:00:41,637
Read, edit, run, check.

17
00:00:41,937 --> 00:00:43,558
The whole visit is one session.

18
00:00:44,058 --> 00:00:45,481
You stop being the messenger.

19
00:00:45,781 --> 00:00:47,859
You watch, and you can stop it at any moment.

20
00:00:48,809 --> 00:00:51,237
It can still be wrong, so give it a test to run.

21
00:00:51,537 --> 00:00:53,417
The mechanic did not get a bigger brain.

22
00:00:53,717 --> 00:00:56,089
He got hands, and a way to check his own work.

23
00:00:56,589 --> 00:00:57,991
Subscribe for the next one.

